      <p>You can shorten or extend this structure depending on your level. The important idea is to give each conversation a small purpose instead of trying to improve every English skill at once.</p>

      <h3>1️⃣ Create a Comfortable Environment</h3>
      <p>Find a quiet space with good lighting and a stable internet connection. Make sure your webcam and microphone work well — clear sound makes communication smoother and more enjoyable.</p>

      <h3>2️⃣ Be Honest About Your Level</h3>
      <p>When you meet someone on the platform, introduce yourself and mention you’re practicing English. Most users are friendly and supportive — honesty helps set the right pace for the conversation.</p>

      <h3>3️⃣ Start with Simple Topics</h3>
      <p>Begin with familiar topics like hobbies, food, travel, or culture. The goal isn’t perfect grammar — it’s connection. Over time, you’ll naturally handle deeper conversations like current events or career goals.</p>

      <h2>4. Overcoming the Fear of Speaking English</h2>

      <h3>Change How You Think About Mistakes</h3>

      <p>Mistakes are useful when they show you exactly what to practice next. Instead of judging an entire conversation as good or bad, identify one specific improvement.</p>

      <div class="table-scroll" style="width:100%;max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;margin:24px 0;">
        <table class="blog-table" style="width:100%;min-width:720px;border-collapse:collapse;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;text-align:left;">What happened</th>
              <th style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;text-align:left;">Don't conclude</th>
              <th style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;text-align:left;">Instead, practice</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">You forgot a word</td>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">"My English is bad."</td>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">Learn the word and two example sentences</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">You misunderstood someone</td>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">"I can't understand English."</td>
